{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTIndex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTIndex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.dt_index_eq_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.dt_index_eq_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L194-L194","doc":"**Content**: the DT invariant `(-1)^{dim moduli} · count` reproduces the\nper-partition binding factor `Δ_λ` for every block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.virtualCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.virtualCount","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L191-L191","doc":"The substrate-forced Behrend-weighted point count of `𝓑_λ`\n(conjecturally the Wedderburn dimension `dim V_λ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.moduliDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.moduliDim","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L188-L188","doc":"The substrate-forced complex dimension of the DT moduli `𝓑_λ`\n(conjecturally the a-function `n(λ)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L185-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DeltaLambdaDTRealization","kind":"class","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L182-L196","doc":"**Open primary conjecture (content-bearing, NO instance).**  The QOU\nsubstrate forces a Donaldson–Thomas / 3d-index moduli `𝓑_λ` whose\nBehrend-signed count is the per-partition binding factor `Δ_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_mixed_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_mixed_sign","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L146-L152","doc":"**Mixed sign from the grading (both horns, packaged).**  Both a positive\nand a negative DT Euler characteristic occur — the positive one from an\neven a-function grade, the negative one from an odd grade.  This is the\n`deltaSign_mixed` fact re-read as the two parities of one graded object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaLambda_not_kl_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaLambda_not_kl_positive","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L137-L144","doc":"**Horn-2 consistency: `Δ_λ` is NOT a KL-positive q-dimension.**  Some block\nhas a strictly negative DT Euler characteristic, so the sequence `(Δ_λ)_λ`\nleaves `ℕ` — it cannot be the `q = 1` value of any KL-positive (non-negative\nLaurent) quantum dimension.  A positivity-violating DT / 3d-index integer,\nexactly as horn 2 concluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.horns_share_one_odd_grade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.horns_share_one_odd_grade","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L125-L135","doc":"**The two horns are ONE phenomenon (the crux).**  A partition with an ODD\na-function grade simultaneously\n  • carries the horn-1 minus sign (`dtEuler < 0`), and\n  • escapes ℕ (`dtEuler < 0`), so it is NOT a KL-positive q-dimension\n    (horn-2's positivity violation).\nBoth are caused by the SAME odd grade — witnessed by `(4,1)`\n(`n(λ) = 1`, `Δ = -4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_neg_iff_odd_grade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_neg_iff_odd_grade","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L116-L123","doc":"**Horn-1 sign leg**: the DT Euler characteristic is negative *iff* the\na-function grade `n(λ)` is odd (all `dim V_λ > 0` at `n = 5`).  The Behrend\n`(-1)^{dim moduli}` sign is negative exactly on odd-dimensional moduli.\n(Oddness written as `n(λ) % 2 = 1` to keep the import surface within the\n`n = 5` anchor's cached olean set.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_magnitude_eq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_magnitude_eq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L109-L114","doc":"**Horn-2 magnitude leg**: `(DT Euler)² = (dim V_λ)²`, i.e. the DT count's\nmagnitude is the Wedderburn dimension.  (Equivalent to\n`binding_magnitude_eq_dim` via the unification.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_eq_deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_eq_deltaLambda","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**THE UNIFICATION (both horns from one object).**  The DT / 3d-index Euler\ncharacteristic of `G_λ` equals the corpus binding factor `Δ_λ`\n(`deltaLambda = deltaSign · dim`).  So the horn-1 sign\n(`deltaSign = (-1)^{n(λ)}`) and the horn-2 magnitude (`|Δ_λ| = dim`) are\nthe sign and the size of a SINGLE Donaldson–Thomas invariant — not two\nindependent ingredients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_eq_sign_times_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.dtEuler_eq_sign_times_dim","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L91-L97","doc":"**The DT Euler characteristic is the sign × magnitude split**: the\nalternating sum collapses (single-degree concentration) to\n`(-1)^{n(λ)} · dim V_λ` — the Behrend sign `(-1)^{dim moduli}` times the\ncount.  Sign and magnitude are the parity and value of ONE graded datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dtEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dtEuler","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L82-L87","doc":"The DT / 3d-index graded Euler characteristic\n`χ(G_λ) = Σ_{k=0}^{n(λ)} (-1)^k · dim (G_λ)_k` — a genuine finite\nalternating sum (the Behrend-weighted count of `𝓑_λ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.gradedDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.gradedDim","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/DeltaLambdaDTIndex.lean#L78-L80","doc":"Graded dimension of `G_λ`: `dim V_λ` concentrated in degree `n(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}